{"seq":3,"slug":"pull-requests-and-review","title":"Pull Requests And Review","docCount":3,"url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-native-git-workflow/pull-requests-and-review","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"small-reviewable-prs","title":"小而可审的 PR","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-native-git-workflow/pull-requests-and-review/small-reviewable-prs","wordCount":1759,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"pr-descriptions-and-intent","title":"PR 描述与意图","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-native-git-workflow/pull-requests-and-review/pr-descriptions-and-intent","wordCount":1733,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"agents-and-the-review-flow","title":"Agent 与评审流程","url":"/h/ai-native-engineering/ai-native-git-workflow/pull-requests-and-review/agents-and-the-review-flow","wordCount":1715,"readingTime":7}],"introMarkdown":"本章讲 PR(Pull Request)作为 agent 时代的把关关口:小而可审的 PR——PR 越小越聚焦,人(和 AI)越审得动、审得住,而非面对一个巨大改动无从下手;PR 描述与意图——好的 PR 描述说清这次改动的目的、做了什么、怎么验证,给评审者必要的上下文;以及 agent 与评审流程——agent 能开 PR、能被 AI/人评审,如何让它顺畅地融入\"产出→评审→合入\"的流程而守住把关。\n"}